# GrantAI — Mission

To give a solo founder and small businesses the same grant-funding
capability normally only affordable to organizations with a dedicated
grants department — by replacing the manual search-score-write-track cycle
with a coordinated system of AI agents that runs continuously, cites its
sources, and never submits anything without explicit founder approval.

## What This Means in Practice

- **Coverage a human can't sustain alone.** Grant Hunter watches approved
  sources continuously, so opportunities aren't missed to bandwidth
  constraints.
- **Judgment before effort.** Nothing gets drafted until it clears
  eligibility and scoring — time is spent only on grants worth pursuing.
- **Draft, never submit.** The system produces work product (research,
  scoring, drafts, budgets) for founder decision-making. Submission authority
  never leaves the founder.
- **Compounding, not repeating.** Every submission — won, lost, or
  withdrawn — feeds back into the scoring model via
  `ContinuousLearning.md`, so the system gets sharper with use.

# GrantAI — Vision

GrantAI matures in three stages:

## Stage 1 — Grant Writing Assistant
A tool you point at a specific opportunity to help research and draft a
proposal. Human-initiated, single-grant-at-a-time.

## Stage 2 — Grant Intelligence Operating System
A standing system with its own knowledge base, scoring engine, and
specialized agents (Finder, Writer, Reviewer, Researcher, Compliance,
Executive Advisor) that can be pointed at a business profile and asked "what
should we pursue this quarter?"

## Stage 3 — Virtual Grant Department (Grant Hunter online)
The system stops waiting to be asked. It watches its approved sources on a
schedule, surfaces new opportunities as they appear, scores and ranks them
automatically, and has draft applications ready for review by the time a
human would have found the opportunity manually. At this stage GrantAI
functions less like software and more like a standing department — one that
never sleeps, never gets tired of checking a source for the tenth time, and
never submits anything without sign-off.

The long-term vision is for GrantAI to become one of BAE's Platform
Capability Modules (BAEOS Vol 12) — usable not just internally for BHI, but
potentially offered as its own product to other small businesses and
contractors facing the same grant-discovery bottleneck.

# GrantAI — Roadmap

**Status:** Draft — founder review required

## Sequencing Logic

Phases are ordered so each one only depends on what's already built:
agents (Phase 2) need governance to exist first (Phase 1); the knowledge
base (Phase 3) has to exist before the intelligence engine (Phase 4) has
anything to score; the intelligence engine has to exist before the
application system (Phase 5) can be triggered by it; engineering (Phase 6)
formalizes what phases 1–5 defined conceptually; operations (Phase 7) governs
the whole system once it's live.

Grant Hunter is intentionally **not** its own phase — it's an enhancement
layer that sits on top of Phases 2–5 once they exist (an agent that calls the
knowledge base, intelligence engine, and application system on a schedule
instead of on-demand). It gets its own agent spec in Phase 2 but can't
actually run until Phases 3–5 are functional.

## Phase 1 — Foundation ✅ (this delivery)
`README.md`, `GOVERNANCE.md`, `MISSION.md`, `VISION.md`, `ROADMAP.md`

## Phase 2 — AI Agent Specifications
- `GrantFinder-Agent.md` — searches sources, surfaces candidates
- `GrantWriter-Agent.md` — drafts proposal narrative
- `GrantReviewer-Agent.md` — QA pass on drafts against funder requirements
- `GrantResearch-Agent.md` — deep-dives a specific funder/opportunity
- `GrantCompliance-Agent.md` — checks eligibility rules, flags legal/reporting obligations
- `ExecutiveGrantAdvisor-Agent.md` — founder-facing summary/recommendation layer
- `GrantHunter-Agent.md` — the autonomous scheduled-sweep agent (flagship enhancement)

## Phase 3 — Knowledge Base
`GrantKnowledge.md`, `FundingOrganizations.md` (the Tier-3 approved source
allow-list Grant Hunter is restricted to), `FederalGrants.md`,
`StateGrants.md`, `CorporateGrants.md`, `FoundationGrants.md`

## Phase 4 — Intelligence Engine
`EligibilityEngine.md`, `MatchingAlgorithm.md`, `ScoringSystem.md`,
`DocumentGeneration.md`, `AutomationWorkflow.md` — this is where Grant
Hunter's scoring threshold and "draft-worthy" logic actually get defined.

## Phase 5 — Application System
`ProposalTemplates.md`, `BusinessProfiles.md`, `BudgetTemplates.md`,
`CommercializationPlans.md`, `ApplicationTracker.md`

## Phase 6 — Engineering
`Architecture.md`, `DatabaseSchema.md`, `API.md`, `Security.md`,
`Testing.md`, `Deployment.md` — this is where Grant Hunter's actual
schedule/trigger mechanism (cron, GitHub Action, etc.) gets specified,
following the same pattern as `sync-agents.yml` elsewhere in the BAE
